<!--
  Anchor: the POSITIVE side stays where it is; the body grows and shrinks the
  other way.

  The mirror of ic_anchor_negative, in the same vocabulary: a solid PIN bar at
  the held edge, an outlined body beside it, and an arrow leaving the free end.
  Mirroring the glyph is the honest way to say the opposite side is held, and it
  mirrors NOTHING about the geometry — the domain has no Mirror, and this is a
  picture.

  Drawn white and tinted at use; see EditorControlStyles.iconButton().
-->
